  "question": {
    "text": "Standing waves are produced by the superposition of two waves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>y</mi></math> are in metre and <math><mi>t</mi></math> is in second. The amplitude of the particle at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>57</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0.54</mn></math>]"
